        {
          "id": "doc-a03984ac4ede::sentence-37",
          "documentId": "doc-a03984ac4ede",
          "text": "For additional information on how and when ballots are verified and tabulated, please visit our description of how the official canvass of the vote is completed.\n",
          "start": 3145,
          "end": 3307,
          "context": "All valid vote-by-mail ballots are counted in every election in California, regardless of the outcome or closeness of any race.  For additional information on how and when ballots are verified and tabulated, please visit our description of how the official canvass of the vote is completed.\n Voting for the First Time\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a03984ac4ede::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-a03984ac4ede",
          "text": "County elections officials mail vote-by-mail ballots to all active registered voters. ",
          "start": 455,
          "end": 541,
          "context": "RECOVERED SOURCE TEXT\n County elections officials mail vote-by-mail ballots to all active registered voters.  Any registered voter may vote using a vote-by-mail ballot instead of going to the polls on Election Day.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a1bd8d9da617::sentence-35",
          "documentId": "doc-a1bd8d9da617",
          "text": "The estimates are rough (some county offices use scales to measure the stacks of paper ballots) and even then, many more votes that were postmarked at the last minute will continue to pour in.\n",
          "start": 3018,
          "end": 3211,
          "context": "Counties are required to begin publishing their estimates of “unprocessed ballots” tomorrow at the end of day.  The estimates are rough (some county offices use scales to measure the stacks of paper ballots) and even then, many more votes that were postmarked at the last minute will continue to pour in.\n After the first uncounted ballot estimates were published after 2016 and 2018 primaries, roughly 35% remained to be tallied. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a03984ac4ede::sentence-17",
          "documentId": "doc-a03984ac4ede",
          "text": "County elections officials mail vote-by-mail ballots to all active registered voters. ",
          "start": 944,
          "end": 1030,
          "context": "Register to Vote\n County elections officials mail vote-by-mail ballots to all active registered voters.  If you believe you are already registered, you can verify your registration online with our “My Voter Status” tool.\n"
        },
        {
